# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.10 — THE DELETER'S NAME IS RESOLVED OUTSIDE THE PLANE GATE
# `Reads.trash/2` resolves the deleter's `Identity.User.full_name` on the ACTING plane, so a tenant
# reads its own member's name clear while an operator without a reveal grant gets a `%Samen.Masked{}`
# (`••••`). This patch resolves that read on a FORCED tenant actor instead — the shape of the classic
# "it renders on the tenant plane, so just decrypt it" fix, which is exactly the leak: name
# resolution is not a rendering detail, it is a PII plane decision.
#
# The defect is silent on the tenant plane (still clear, still correct) and silent in every
# non-masking assertion: the row still lists, still restores, still says who. Only the operator-plane
# red path distinguishes a masked name from a leaked one — which is what the failing assertion reads.
#
# Aimed at the RESOLVER'S PLANE only. The org filter on the identity read, the audit read, the label
# fallbacks and the row projection are all untouched.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the operator plane without a grant renders
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
@@ -267,7 +267,11 @@
         |> Ash.read!(authorize?: false)
 
       users
-      |> resolve(mount, scope, user_resource)
+      |> resolve(
+        mount,
+        %Samen.Scope{actor: Map.put(actor_of(scope), :plane, :tenant)},
+        user_resource
+      )
       |> Enum.reduce(%{}, fn user, acc ->
         case display_name(user) do
           nil -> acc
